{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "אתה ואהרן", :translit "atah ve'aharon", :gloss "you and Aaron"} {:he "יצרנהו כאישון עינו", :translit "yitzarnehu ke'ishon eino", :gloss "He formed them as the apple of His eye"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :sofei-tevot, :phrase "אליצור ומסיים בעינן", :spells ""} {:kind :other, :note "Ba'al HaTurim reads the princes' names Elitzur...Pagiel as encoding the phrase 'yitzarnehu ke'ishon eino' through the opening and closing letters of the list"}], :frame {:text "The census in Ki Tissa (Exodus 30:11–12) was counted by Moses alone, without Aaron's participation. The calf was made 'through Aaron' in the sense that he fashioned it (Exodus 32:4, 24). The verse 'He kept them as the apple of His eye' (Deuteronomy 32:10) uses the word כאישון, which the Ba'al HaTurim links to the cloud through which God guided Israel (Numbers 9:15–22).", :sources ["Exodus 30:11–12" "Exodus 32:4" "Exodus 32:24" "Deuteronomy 32:10" "Numbers 9:15–22"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :sofei-tevot, :phrase "אליצור ומסיים בעינן", :spells "", :letters ["ר" "ם" "ן"], :by :selah, :order :mismatch} {:kind :other, :note "Ba'al HaTurim reads the princes' names Elitzur...Pagiel as encoding the phrase 'yitzarnehu ke'ishon eino' through the opening and closing letters of the list", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:26:40.785684166Z", :model "glm-5.2"}